WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.826
Hi! Don't panic when you meet a word you don't know in a test. The sentence often hides clues to its meaning. Today let's be word detectives!

2
00:00:11.976 --> 00:00:19.794
Look at this sentence: The hike was so strenuous that we had to rest often. You might not know the word strenuous.

3
00:00:19.944 --> 00:00:24.138
Look for clues. It says we had to rest often.

4
00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:30.858
Now look at the options: very easy, very tiring, very short, very noisy.

5
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:39.882
Needing lots of rest means it was tiring, so strenuous means very tiring. Cross out the options that don't fit.

6
00:00:40.032 --> 00:00:49.722
Clue one is an example. She loves citrus fruits, such as oranges and lemons. So citrus fruits are fruits like oranges and lemons.

7
00:00:49.872 --> 00:00:59.466
Clue two is contrast. Although the puppy was timid at first, it soon became playful. Timid is the opposite of playful, so it means shy.

8
00:00:59.616 --> 00:01:09.858
Clue three is cause and effect. He was drenched because he forgot his umbrella. No umbrella means he got very wet, so drenched means completely wet.

9
00:01:10.008 --> 00:01:20.178
Clue four is an explanation. The room was spotless, without a single speck of dust. So spotless means perfectly clean.

10
00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:24.354
Step one: read the whole sentence, not just the word.

11
00:01:24.504 --> 00:01:29.418
Step two: find the clues, and guess the meaning in your own words.

12
00:01:29.568 --> 00:01:37.698
Step three: put each option back into the sentence and read it. Choose the one that makes the most sense.

13
00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:45.090
Watch out! Some pupils see elated, think it has something to do with being late, and pick the wrong answer!

14
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:54.666
Words that look alike aren't always related. Use the sentence: She was elated when she won the prize. Winning means she was very happy.

15
00:01:54.816 --> 00:02:02.754
Remember: trust the clues, not the look of the word, and check by putting it back into the sentence.

16
00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:14.034
Your turn! Tim was reluctant to swim because the water was icy. What does reluctant mean? Pause and think.

17
00:02:14.184 --> 00:02:22.098
It means unwilling. The water was icy, so he didn't want to swim. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:22.248 --> 00:02:34.506
Another one! Dad was furious when he saw the broken vase, but he calmed down later. What does furious mean? Pause and think.

19
00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:44.058
It means very angry. Later he calmed down, so before that he must have been very angry. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:56.010
Last one! The shy girl, unlike her outgoing brother, rarely spoke in class. What does outgoing mean? Pause and think.

21
00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:04.434
It means friendly and sociable. Unlike tells us it's the opposite of shy. Did you get it right?

22
00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:18.282
Remember: when you meet a new word, read the whole sentence and look for clues: examples, contrast, cause and effect, and explanations. Guess first, then check each option in the sentence.

23
00:03:18.432 --> 00:03:23.346
Be a word detective the next time you read a storybook!

